    curl -sL https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt > LICENSE

Replace "[Your Name]" above with your name or organization.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHY AGPL-3.0?

Varsha bundles animated GIFs from ExerciseDB
(https://github.com/ExerciseDB/exercisedb-api), which is licensed under
AGPL-3.0. The AGPL is "viral" — any work that incorporates AGPL data or
code must itself be distributed under AGPL-3.0 (or compatible). That makes
this whole project AGPL.

Other bundled data:
  • yuhonas/free-exercise-db — public domain (Unlicense), AGPL-compatible.
  • Exercise prescriptions and form cues in WorkoutData.swift — original
    work, contributed under AGPL-3.0 along with the rest of the project.

If you don't want AGPL, run the fetcher with --frames-only to skip
ExerciseDB entirely; the two-frame animator from free-exercise-db is
public domain and imposes no restrictions, so you'd be free to relicense
the project under MIT, Apache-2.0, or anything else.
